---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProjectLinks from '../components/ProjectLinks.astro';
import { getPhase } from '../data/phases';

const financeColor = getPhase('finance').color;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Domains - projecttrack.dev"
  description="A data science career has two axes: domain and function. See where the track's projects fit."
>
  <article class="domains">
    <p class="eyebrow">Domains</p>
    <h1>Choose your lane</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      A data science career has two axes. <strong>Domain</strong> is where your data lives: finance, health, retail,
      sports. <strong>Function</strong> is what you do to it: analyst, ML engineer, researcher. A role is one point
      on each axis, not just a domain.
    </p>

    <section class="finance-lane" style={`--lane-color: ${financeColor};`}>
      <p class="lane-label">The deep lane</p>
      <h2>Finance</h2>
      <p><ProjectLinks orders={[8, 9, 10, 11]} /> are the finance lane of the main track: market forecasting, credit risk, a data pipeline, and a document assistant built on filings. This is the domain the site teaches to depth.</p>
      <p class="why">Why finance specifically: it's my own lane, the one I know most about, so it's the one I can actually teach properly.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Tech and product</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>A/B test analysis</li>
          <li>A recommendation system</li>
          <li>User churn or engagement prediction</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="skills">Same skills as <ProjectLinks orders={[1]} /> (tabular ML) and <ProjectLinks orders={[4]} /> (clustering), the same logic behind a recommendation system.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Health</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Chest X-ray classification</li>
          <li>Lung-function decline from CT scans</li>
          <li>Disease prediction from tabular records</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="skills">Same skills as <ProjectLinks orders={[5, 6, 7]} /> (image classification) and <ProjectLinks orders={[1]} /> (tabular ML).</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Marketing and retail</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Customer churn prediction</li>
          <li>Customer segmentation</li>
          <li>Customer lifetime value prediction</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="skills">Same skills as <ProjectLinks orders={[1]} /> (tabular ML) and <ProjectLinks orders={[4]} /> (clustering).</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Sports</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Match-outcome prediction</li>
          <li>Player-performance models</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="skills">Same skills as <ProjectLinks orders={[1]} /> (tabular ML) and <ProjectLinks orders={[8]} /> (working with data over time).</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="closing">
      Finance is the lane this site teaches to depth. The others show the shape of the work and a real project to
      start on, not a full curriculum. Every non-finance example maps back to a function skill the track already
      teaches: this page is a different lens on the same 12 projects, not separate content.
    </p>

    <section class="certifications">
      <p class="eyebrow">Go deeper</p>
      <h2>Certifications</h2>
      <p class="lede small">
        Certifications help you clear resume screens and learn in a structured way, but the projects on this track
        are what actually prove you can do the work.
      </p>
      <p class="lede small">
        If you want a credential on top of the projects, here is where each lane usually points. These are starting
        points, not a definitive list.
      </p>

      <div class="card-grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Finance</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>CFA</strong> (Chartered Financial Analyst): investment analysis and portfolio management, the standard credential on the buy side.</li>
            <li><strong>FRM</strong> (Financial Risk Manager): measuring and managing financial risk, common on trading and risk desks.</li>
            <li><strong>CAIA</strong> (Chartered Alternative Investment Analyst): alternative assets like hedge funds, private equity, and real assets.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Tech and product</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>AWS Certified AI Practitioner</strong> or <strong>Microsoft Azure AI Fundamentals (AI-900)</strong>: entry-level starting points for AI.</li>
            <li><strong>AWS Certified Machine Learning Engineer Associate</strong>: building and operationalizing ML in production on AWS.</li>
            <li><strong>Google Cloud Professional Machine Learning Engineer</strong>: the full ML lifecycle on Google Cloud, one of the most technical mainstream ML certs.</li>
            <li><strong>Microsoft Azure AI Engineer Associate (AI-102)</strong>: building AI solutions with Azure OpenAI and Azure services.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Health</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>CHDA</strong> (Certified Health Data Analyst, AHIMA): analyzing health data specifically, not just data in general.</li>
            <li><strong>CPHIMS</strong> (Certified Professional in Healthcare Information and Management Systems, HIMSS): healthcare information systems more broadly.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Marketing and retail</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Google Analytics Certification</strong>: measuring and interpreting web and product analytics.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="skills">The general analytics certificates listed under Tech and product apply here too.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Sports</h3>
          <p class="skills">
            There is no one standard credential here the way finance has the CFA. The general data and ML
            certificates above are the practical starting point. Knowledge of the sport itself matters as much as
            any certificate.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .domains {
    width: min(100% - 48px, 860px);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-block: 64px 120px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(30px, 4.2vw, 46px);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    color: var(--color-heading);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0 0 48px;
  }
  .lede.small {
    font-size: 16px;
    margin: 0 0 32px;
  }
  .lede strong {
    color: var(--color-heading);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .finance-lane {
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--lane-color) 30%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--lane-color) 6%, transparent);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 28px 30px 30px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .lane-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--lane-color);
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .finance-lane h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 26px;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--color-heading);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .finance-lane p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .finance-lane .why {
    margin-top: 14px;
    padding-top: 14px;
    border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--lane-color) 25%, transparent);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .card-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 600px) {
    .card-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
  .card-grid > .card:last-child:nth-child(odd) {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }
  .card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-card-bg);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 24px 24px 26px;
  }
  .card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 19px;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--color-heading);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .card ul {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .card li {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .card p {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .card .skills {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .closing {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0 0 72px;
  }

  .certifications h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 32px);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    color: var(--color-heading);
  }
</style>
